ee variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3})=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{6}{5}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot 6+(-15)\\cdot 3+28\\cdot 5}{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{5}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-60-45+140}{36+9+25}b \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{70}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1043 #edb/ref 17592186417873 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1043 #edb/ref 17592186417874 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1043 #edb/ref 17592186417875 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1043 #edb/ref 17592186417876 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1043 #edb/ref 17592186417877 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1045 "Projecting Vectors Onto One-Dimensional Subspaces" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1046 #edb/ref 17592186417877 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048893 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417838 1053 #uuid "77f1e5a5-6e60-5f32-84e4-cd4e652f94b4" 13194139534294