nd{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3\\cdot (2{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=5{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 5+(-5)\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 1}{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-60\\,}{\\,\\,\\,30\\,}b \\\\  & =-2b \\\\  & =-2[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417870 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417868 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417870 1069 "q-39728" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417870 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417870 1071 "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $u$ and $\\text{Span}{w}.$" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417870 1072 #uuid "3155d938-fdbf-5fc6-acad-f273132af9c1" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417870 1074 "The distance between the vector $u$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}{w}$ is given by $‖u-\\overset{^}{u}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{u}$ in the orthogonal projection of $u$ onto $\\text{Span}{w}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $u$ onto $\\text{Span}{w}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,u & =\\frac{w\\cdot u}{w\\cdot w}w \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 6}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}w \\\\  & =\\frac{8+2+4+6}{4+1+4+1}w \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{10}w \\\\  & =2w \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u-\\overset{^}{u}‖ & =\\sqrt{({u}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{u}}_{1})^{2}+({u}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{u}}_{2})^{2}+({u}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{u}}_{3})^{2}+({u}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{u}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4-4)^{2}+(2-2)^{2}+(-2-(-4))^{2}+(6-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+0+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417871 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417866 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417871 1069 "q-40381" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417871 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417871 1071 "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ then $z=$" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417871 1072 #uuid "3365c089-bf35-5299-ad47-d460e03b5d34" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417871 1074 "![](images/d8/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{a}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 7+(-3)(-6)+1\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6+21+18+1}{4+9+9+1}a \\\\  & =\\frac{46}{23}a \\\\  & =2a \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}{a}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}{a},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417872 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417864 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417872 1069 "q-86750" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417872 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417872 1071 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417872 1072 #uuid "ded73fa4-75de-583c-84b7-7ec2dfdeee44" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417872 1074 "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-7{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(-7{x}_{3})-3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-4{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{3} \\\\ -7{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot (-4)+(-13)\\cdot (-7)+1\\cdot (1)}{(-4)^{2}+(-7)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{132}{66}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417873 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417874 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417873 1062 #uuid "62a4d3df-d96d-5ff1-bcdc-6b9572844deb" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417873 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417870 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417874 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417875 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417874 1062 #uuid "7d14fc8b-c658-5579-8cfd-ea6f41729396" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417874 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417871 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417875 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417876 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417875 1062 #uuid "962d37cc-84fe-5f22-9f18-fe787b5d8f8a" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417875 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417872 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417876 1062 #uuid "bdf29d7e-7c25-5367-b984-2503f598b196" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417876 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417869 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417877 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417873 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417877 1062 #uuid "c8ab4513-610d-50c5-a113-b2b14f2cbf31" 13194139534294 17592186045417 true] [17592186417877 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134234 13194139534294 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-77f1e5a5-6e60-5f32-84e4-cd4e652f94b4" 17592186417838 "answer-0